<!--
  Copyright (C) 2026 The X-ROM Project
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Declares AVF to PackageManager.

  FEATURE_VIRTUALIZATION_FRAMEWORK is the single authoritative signal that AVF
  exists on this device:
    * VirtualMachineManager.getSystemService() returns non-null only when it is
      present (below API level 34 the service does not exist at all).
    * PackageManager.hasSystemFeature(FEATURE_VIRTUALIZATION_FRAMEWORK) is the
      version-independent probe recommended by AOSP for apps.
    * The AVF VTS/CTS suites (MicrodroidTestApp, VirtualizationTestCases) skip
      or fail based on it.

  Protected-VM capability is deliberately NOT declared here. It is a boot-time
  hardware/firmware fact, communicated by the bootloader through the bootconfig
  key androidboot.hypervisor.protected_vm.supported=true and surfaced as
  ro.boot.hypervisor.protected_vm.supported. Declaring pKVM support in a static
  XML would let a build claim an isolation property the silicon cannot provide,
  which is exactly the failure mode X-ROM exists to prevent.
-->
<config>
    <feature name="android.software.virtualization_framework" />
</config>
